{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792312279,"nonce":"sO0TR4drn7XpUpEscblf7qiPJH0=","title":"A wake from a worker thread that cannot be delivered ends the thread","message":"`Work.notify` calls the host's wake from whatever thread queued work. In a page, from a worker thread, that call into xwindow.wasm throws (Ash 191b6e9), outside any handler, and the runtime aborts the thread (\"hlp_throw called without active trap\"): the first texture compression's result handed back and the program trapped.\n\n**Fix**\n\nA wake from another thread is a hint. `Work.notify` catches a failure of it, so the work stays queued and the thread goes on. The web host's wake does nothing today; when it does, the same call will work.","files":null}]}